OBS ev=isolated_socket:codex-p2-37028.sock :: Windows PowerShell: workspace create, pane split p2, new-window p3, split-window p4, and each distinct computed output marker passed with exit=0; isolated kill-server exit=0.
OBS ev=isolated_socket:codex-p2-36884.sock :: Windows cmd.exe fallback: the same three creation paths executed distinct markers expanded from their own pane IDs; all commands/waits and isolated kill-server exit=0. Temporary isolated config/state removed.
NR :: Non-Windows shell execution and a real attached interactive TUI were not exercised; the latter was tested through State::exec with a test client. Legacy non-PowerShell startup submission is asynchronous because the TUI command executor holds the state lock; a later submit failure is logged. The existing release daemon was not rebuilt, restarted or killed; it does not include these changes until integration/restart.
